Mark the take side of the arbitration lock

run-372 shows B Arm as the last service name and then only U1 U2T U3 from other
threads: the name is written before the console print, so the thread stops
somewhere after it -- in the print or in lockForArbitration, which had no marks
at all.  L1 before the global take and L2 once it is held separates a thread
waiting for the lock from a console that stopped printing.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index a2a6fd8..0673f28 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -1693,8 +1693,13 @@ IOService::lockForArbitration( bool isSuccessRequired )
 
 	enum { kPutOnFreeQueue, kPutOnActiveQueue, kPutOnWaitingQueue } action;
 
+	/* nio: the lock side of the arbitration had no marks, so a thread that
+	 * stops here looks exactly like a console failure -- the panel shows
+	 * 'B Arm' and then nothing.  L1 before the take, L2 once it is held. */
+	nio_u_mark("\nL1");
 	// lock global access
 	IOTakeLock( gArbitrationLockQueueLock );
+	nio_u_mark(" L2");
 
 	// obtain an unused queue element
 	if (!queue_empty( &gArbitrationLockQueueFree )) {
